# AST conformance engine pins

## Root cause

The scheduled AST workflow measures reviewed engine revisions from `resources/engine-pins.json`. Its JavaScript reference build also needs the matching dependency in `package.json`. Those revisions precede merged AST fixes in carve-js, carve-php, and carve-rs, so the workflow measures old behavior. The new revisions also make two lint drift declarations stale: the engines now agree on those rows.

## Change

Align the repository's reviewed engine state with current main: advance the three engine pins with `scripts/set-engine-pin.mjs`, update the JavaScript npm lockfile, and remove drift declarations where the new builds agree. Keep the Ruby pin and the conformance oracle unchanged. Run the AST workflow at these revisions, then file engine-specific bugs with reproductions for any remaining divergence.

## Scope

The pins select complete engine builds used across the corpus and all AST shards. They do not special-case any listed shape, document, or expected tree.
